/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  trayEfficiency04_yanagi08_165kPa  --  the EFFICIENCY OF A SIEVE TRAY COMPUTED FROM ITS
  GEOMETRY, held against a commercial-scale measurement it was not fitted to
  (DEV.md 4c C329).  Cyclohexane / n-heptane at 165 kPa, total reflux.

  THE TRAY: FRI's 8 % hole-area sieve tray, the one the paper compares against
  (Sakata & Yanagi 1979): IDENTICAL to the 14 % tray (same column, 12.7 mm
  holes, weir, downcomers) except the panels -- holes on 38.1 mm pitch, about
  8 % of the bubbling area.  ONLY holeAreaFraction and the orifice
  coefficient that follows from it differ from the 14 % case.
  Source: Yanagi & Sakata, Ind. Eng. Chem. Process Des. Dev. 21 (1982) 712.
  The pair of this case is trayEfficiency03_yanagi14_165kPa (14 %): the two differ in the open area
  and in nothing else.

  THE MODEL.  The stages stay equilibrium stages; each tray's Murphree
  efficiency is computed from its geometry, its own traffic and the transport
  properties of its two phases -- the AIChE Bubble-Tray Manual correlations
  for sieve trays (Treybal 3ed Eqs 6.38, 6.51-6.64), eddy diffusion along the
  liquid path, and the entrainment loss near flood (Colburn with Fair's median
  entrainment, Perry 9ed Eqs 14-98, 14-99) at the tray's approach to flood
  (Fair / Lygeros, with Perry's open-area correction below 10 %).  The tray
  pressure drop is Bolles & Fair's (Perry 9ed Eqs 14-100..14-109).

  MEASURED INPUTS (the paper): the tray geometry (Table I); the liquid
    viscosity 0.23 mPa s (Table II, 165 kPa -- the package carries no
    liquid viscosity for these components, so the paper's own average enters
    Wilke-Chang); the column pressure.
  ASSUMED: the reboiler liquid, 0.29 mol fraction cyclohexane (Table III gives
    0.284 and 0.294 for the two runs it lists; the other points' compositions
    are not published); every point of the sweep uses it.
  ESTIMATED PROPERTIES: vapour pressure (Antoine fits to CoolProp), ideal
    liquid, vapour viscosity (Chung, Vc from Zc(omega)), vapour diffusivity
    (Fuller; the diffusion volumes, Poling 5ed Table 11-1, are added to the
    case's own component records), liquid diffusivity (Wilke-Chang at
    infinite dilution, combined linearly, Poling 5ed Eq 11-10.2), liquid
    density (Rackett on the record's Vliq), surface tension (Brock-Bird).
  FITTED PARAMETERS: NONE.
  HELD-OUT POINTS: all -- the eight 8 % points at 165 kPa of Figure 12 and the six of Figure 13
    (DIGITISED; see trayEfficiency02 for where the 8 % tables are).
    The comparison table is in docs/design/c329-ratebased-first-delivery.md.
  WHAT WAS CHOSEN AFTER SEEING DATA, said so: the pressure-drop route.  The
    default (Sinnott) gave 0.79 kPa per tray on run 628 against the measured
    0.393; Bolles & Fair was then implemented from Perry and gives 0.41.  No
    number inside either correlation was touched.
  IN-SAMPLE OR NOT: the AIChE correlations were built from the AIChE research
    programme of the 1950s; Perry 9ed p. 13-38 notes FRI data were then
    available only to FRI members, so these points are out of the
    correlation's sample.  (Zuiderweg 1982 would NOT be: his interfacial area
    was fitted to these very FRI data -- Klemola & Ilme 1996, p. 4581.)

  WHAT THE MODEL CANNOT SEE: hole area.  The AIChE transfer units carry none,
  so the open area reaches the efficiency only through the flood approach
  (entrainment) and the pressure drop.  Weeping is not modelled, so the
  low-load fall-off of the measured efficiency is not predicted.  The sweep
  stops below the load at which Fair's entrainment correlation passes psi = 1
  (the model's own entrainment flood).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       totalReflux;

        operation
        {
            nStages        11;          // 10 trays + the reboiler
            P              165 kPa;
            condenser      { type total; }

            totalReflux
            {
                fFactor        1.47;    // swept; (m/s)(kg/m3)^0.5, reboiler vapour on the tower area
                specifiedAt    reboiler;
                composition
                {
                    cyclohexane    0.29;
                    nHeptane       0.71;
                }
            }

            efficiency
            {
                model            AIChE;
                lightKey         cyclohexane;
                liquidViscosity  2.3e-4;   // Pa s, Yanagi & Sakata Table II, 165 kPa
                entrainment      FairMedian;
            }

            hydraulics
            {
                trayType               sieve;
                pressureDropModel      BollesFair;   // Perry 9ed 14-100..14-109
                diameter               1.2;      // m  (Table I)
                traySpacing            0.610;    // m  (Table I)
                weirHeight             0.0508;   // m  (Table I, efficiency runs)
                holeDiameter           0.0127;   // m  (Table I)
                holeAreaFraction       0.0808;   // 8 % of the 0.859 m2 bubbling area = 0.0687 m2, over 0.851 m2 active
                downcomerAreaFraction  0.1238;   // 0.14 m2 / 1.131 m2 (Table I)
                weirLengthFraction     0.7833;   // 0.940 m / 1.2 m (Table I)
                orificeCoefficient     0.651;    // Perry 9ed Eq 14-102a: 0.74 A_h/A_a + exp(0.29 (1.5/12.7) - 0.56)
            }
        }
    }
);
